each related feature paired with an association end of the type using a notation of the form e references f or e
::> f, where e is the name of an association end and f is the qualified name of a related feature. In this case, the
name of each association end must appear exactly once in the list of connector end declarations.
A special notation can be used for a binary connector, in which the source related feature is referenced after the
keyword from, and the target related feature is referenced after the keyword to.

