Functions are behaviors (see 7.4.7 ) with one out parameter designated as the result parameter. Functions classify
evaluations (see 9.2.6.2.4 ), which are kinds of performances that produce results as values of the result parameter.
Like all behaviors, functions can change things, often referred to as "side effects". A pure function is one that has no

